ry patient  and and also charitable to  you know put up with the comings and  goings and modifying their lives and  helping out in their ways it was a blur  but i don't i don't remember feeling  burdened at all by having other people  in our home  you know just it was like more siblings  except  they're more like on the friend scale  than sibling  all the while karen and husband gary  were busy raising their boys  involved in their church the pta boy  scouts  and taking family vacations karen has  stumbled over some hurdles of her own  losing her gift basket business when the  economy tanked in 2008  and recovering from gambling addiction  in overcoming that i do think i've  become  a better person because i'm more  empathetic  sympathetic i understand better  that people need second chances and  they need a leg up when the next door  neighbor's home was damaged in a fire  karen invited them in for a drink of  water  and told them to stay until the house  was rebuilt  another spontaneous offer of help that  made a lasting difference in someone's  life  you know we were glad to be able to do  that for them and we still stay in touch  with  all the people that have come and gone  out of our home and  and they all are much more successful  and stable than they were in that period  of time  now watching their sons grow up to have  families of their own  karen knows they see the good in making  room in your life  for others i'm super grateful that she  set that example for us because  um it has certainly influenced our  choices to  to give back and and to look outside of  ourselves  and that's why karen eddington is our  remarkable woman  sheri swensk 8 news now
 

